[4] Proof readout
  1. The residue-terminal quotient has exactly two boundary/open
     collisions on the tested full bank.  They are AP and GW against
     open impostors.
  2. In those collisions, the boundary rows are exactly the AP/GW
     arc-Cech cycle: closed arc beta=(1,1), open arc beta=(6,0),
     zero safe topes, and six owner-current sums 0 mod 14.
  3. Every open cohabitant in those two fibers has closed arc beta1=0
     and at least four safe topes.  This gives a topology-first
     separator for equality atoms before arithmetic route labels.
  4. The coarse ET+unit gate has no boundary/open mixing.  Its 15
     remaining route-mixed fibers contain 38 packets, all open, all
     closed beta1=0.  Route mixing here is harmless for the direct
     LRC predicate and can be scheduled later by magnitude/covering
     certificates.
  5. Candidate theorem: primitive zero-open packets must carry the
     AP/GW arc-boundary cycle, or else the arc topology emits positive
     safe topes and the coarse ET+unit gate is allowed to forget the
     exact route while preserving status.
